# Constraint search and nondeterminism

```elixir
Mix.install([
  {:swi_elixir, path: Path.expand("..", __DIR__)},
  {:kino, "== 0.19.0"}
])
```

## Introduction

N-queens asks for one queen in each column with no attacking rows or diagonals.
This notebook uses SWI-Prolog's [CLP(FD) library](https://www.swi-prolog.org/pldoc/man?section=clpfd)
to state the constraints, then lets Elixir decide how many solutions to consume.
The board displays are built from the returned placements.

Evaluate from top to bottom in a local Livebook runtime on a [supported platform](../README.md#platforms-and-native-bundles).
Setup installs this checkout, its bundled SWI runtime, and Kino; the first dependency installation needs
network access. All search data is defined below.

